{"chunk_id": "3ac83ed79c36", "text": "Arjuna recounts the climax of his mysterious battle with the hunter who had challenged him. Despite unleashing volleys of arrows and divine weapons\u2014including those of Wind, Varuna, and even Brahma\u2014the opponent effortlessly absorbs or nullifies them, changing forms and overwhelming Arjuna in physical combat. When Arjuna collapses, the hunter reveals his true identity: the god Shiva, accompanied by Uma. Pleased by Arjuna\u2019s courage and persistence, Shiva grants him the terrifying Pasupata weapon, warning it must never be used against ordinary mortals. Soon afterward the Lokapalas and Indra appear, bestow further celestial weapons, and invite Arjuna to heaven. Guided by Matali, Arjuna travels to Amaravati, learns divine arts and weaponry, and is eventually tasked by Indra to destroy the powerful ocean\u2011dwelling demons, the Nivata\u2011Kavachas, as his preceptor\u2019s fee.\nArjuna receives the Pasupata weapon from Shiva, is welcomed by the gods, travels to heaven with Matali, trains under Indra, and is tasked to slay the Nivata-Kavachas.\nThemes: divine weapons, Arjuna's ascension to heaven, trial and divine favor, training under Indra, heroic quest", "vector": [0.010938831605017185, -0.005011065863072872, -0.012560159899294376, 0.01867605373263359, -0.008154526352882385, 0.03278229013085365, -0.027131587266921997, -0.01729416288435459, -0.019715894013643265, -0.01938752271234989, 0.010364184156060219, 0.007224144414067268, 0.006085109896957874, -0.0032289735972881317, 0.004097786266356707, 0.016774244606494904, 0.04523299261927605, -0.022766999900341034, 0.011554526165127754, -0.025544464588165283, -0.015556537546217442, 0.005920925177633762, 0.007347282953560352, 0.013162171468138695, -0.008722333237528801, 0.011828168295323849, 0.004258550703525543, -0.033630579710006714, 0.006023540627211332, -0.008907041512429714, -0.003683903021737933, -0.003447887022048235, -0.002175452420488, 0.004532192833721638, -0.02176